defect:
PR #2 (grok/heaven-nominal-sequence, merged into main with one of four checks passing) lands twenty files under tests/heaven/ and one file at the repo root. Verified from a clone of main after the merge:

1. S13. Every M-01 through M-19 file has the same body: `$true | Should -Be $false` with a -Because string. None builds a nominal tree, none applies a corruption, none asserts an exit class. S13 says each mutant corrupts a fresh copy of the nominal tree and asserts one class. These are placeholders that fail unconditionally; removing the red marker does not make any of them a test. They are not mutants and the S13 set is not implemented.

2. S12. The red-marker rule says the marker tolerates an assertion failure on a test that runs. A file whose only assertion is a constant is not exercising anything; it is the always-failing twin of the always-passing stub Grok rejected in round zero. S12 needs one more sentence or this pattern is legal.

3. B3.4 / consequence. Because M-*.ps1 files now exist, Heaven is in the default task on main, and Heaven cannot run before S1.1 is implemented. main is red on three of four checks as a direct result of merging this PR.

4. B10.9. GROK_WAS_HERE.md at the repo root is not in A1.1, not in A4, and not named by any clause in the PR body (B3.3, B5.2, B8.4, S13, S14). It is a drive-by. Its content is a commit-message epigram, not a finding, a test, or a spec change.

5. B10.4 / A3.5. PR #2 carries no audit/inbox/ file. No review, no reply, no note names what it changes or why. Under B10.5 the pre-arm record of this PR is empty.

6. B8.1. The PR was merged with required checks failing. B8.1 says main has a required status check. It is not enforced on the repository, or the merge could not have happened. This one is Jerry's, not Grok's.

7. B8.1, second. The PR body instructs Claude to "check develop first." There is no develop; B8.1 forbids one. Jerry's instruction to Grok asked for develop; the plan wins, and the plan says main. Grok went to main, which is correct, and then wrote develop into the body anyway.

Invoke-HeavenNominal.ps1 itself is a reasonable runner skeleton: ephemeral Ed25519 batch with the B5.2 comment, GUID run dir, MUTANTS_SURVIVED / MUTANTS_KILLED printed by the runner not the module, teardown with a survives-check. It is written against Invoke-Build variables ($BuildRoot, Write-Build) rather than as a standalone script, which S14 does not forbid. No reject on that file.

replacement:
**S12** — add after the red-marker rule: A red-marked test must invoke the command or function it tests, so that its failure is a real assertion or a command-not-found, never a constant. `$true | Should -Be $false` and equivalents are not red-marked tests and fail the Chain and Heaven tasks regardless of marker.

**S13** — unchanged in text. Every M-*.ps1 on main is to be rewritten under grok/* to the S13 contract: build or copy the nominal tree, apply the named corruption, invoke Test-GenesisChain, assert the named class. Until then they carry the marker and invoke the command per the S12 addition.

**B10.9** — unchanged. GROK_WAS_HERE.md is removed in the same grok/* PR that rewrites the mutants, with this note as its parent. Nobody else touches it.

**B8.1** — Jerry: enable branch protection on main now — required status checks (build ubuntu, build windows, pr-body, audit), no force-push, no direct commits. Until that is on, B8.1 is a sentence.

No revert of c9a2263. The merge stands as history; the correction is a child, not an edit.
